One Important Distinction
Students often confuse sliding window, prefix sum, and Kadane because all three can involve subarrays.

Think of them like this:

Sliding Window
You're maintaining a window:

[ 2  3  1  2 ]
  ↑        ↑
 left     right

Usually useful when the window has some constraint.

Prefix Sum
You're asking:

"What is the sum between these two positions?"

prefix[right + 1] - prefix[left]

Kadane
You're asking:

"Which contiguous subarray has the maximum sum?"

currentSum = Math.max(nums[i],
                      currentSum + nums[i]);

